---
description: DevKit project rules
alwaysApply: true
---
- Project: native macOS SwiftUI app "DevKit", arm64, macOS 14+, Swift Package (no Xcode, no .xcodeproj).
- Build with `swift build -c release --arch arm64` or `./build.sh`. Fix all errors and warnings before finishing.
- Edit files directly. Never reprint whole files. Reply in 3 lines or fewer.
- No stubs, no TODOs. If something is impossible, say so in one line.
- Every tool = one file in Sources/DevKit/Tools/ + one line in ToolRegistry.swift.
- Pure logic lives in Sources/DevKitCore (no SwiftUI imports) so it is testable.
- Heavy work runs off the main thread. Never force-unwrap external input.
- Prefer Apple frameworks. Third-party only: Yams, swift-markdown, SwiftSoup.
- Read @SPEC.md only when a batch needs it. Do not re-read unrelated files.
